  "important_notes": "doWrite() in ConsoleIO maps IOInterface verbosity constants to Symfony VERBOSITY_* via verbosityMap, optionally prepends memory/time debug info or timestamps, routes stderr to ConsoleOutputInterface::getErrorOutput(). doOverwrite() uses backspace chars (\\x08) to overwrite previous terminal output. BufferIO is used in tests and CI scenarios. NullIO is used when no output is desired (e.g., scripted non-interactive runs).",

